            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "4e3c3945-0bf4-4040-9735-546541b27a50",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Less.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we learned that on a ruler the marks always keep the same distance between the numbers, and that a number that comes after another is greater than it. On the other hand, a number that comes before another is always smaller than it.\n\n**A useful tip:** the open side of the comparison symbol — greater (>) or smaller (<) — always faces the larger number. Test it with **21 > 20**: the opening faces 21.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
